    <body>
      <div type="work" n="69">
        <pb n="112"/>
        <head>69 — iv — VI. — <quote>Thy knowledge hath been admired by me</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">Who is there who could fitly praise the boundless greatness of thy mercifulness, <persName>Christ</persName>, God? who even in the very sufferings, mean and vile and very lowly, which thou enduredst voluntarily on our behalf showedst that thou art Creator <pb n="113"/> and Lord and renovating<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> artificer of this universe. For thou tookest upon thee for the sake of our salvation to be crowned with a crown<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> of thorns; [and by this means thou didst signifiy<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> that, having gathered and compressed together the sins of the whole circuit of the world, and having taken these upon thyself, thou didst carry them up<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> with thee upon the revered Cross. Wherefore also thou tarest and blottedst out the handwriting<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> of sin that was laid upon us; and again being mocked thou heldest a reed in thy hand, that thereby thou mightest strengthen the rod of our sway<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> that had been weakened, whereby we have been set to rule over all that are on earth; and, having gone down in thy soul to Sheol, thou didst free them that were there bound<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/>; and the multitudes of the hosts<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> that are in heaven [wondered and were astonished at<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/> thy wisdom rich in help<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a11" target="#n11" n="11"/> through the dispensation [on our behalf<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a12" target="#n12" n="12"/>. Lord, who hast enlightened and adorned with knowledge all creatures above and below, praise to thee!</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 112, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. cxxxviii, 6 LXX.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>renovator</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 2</orig></choice> Matth. xxvii, 27-31 <quote>Then the soldiers..... and smote on his head.... to be crucified.</quote></note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>signifying</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 4</orig></choice> 1 Pet. ii, 24 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 5</orig></choice> Marg. <foreign xml:lang="grc">χειρόγραφα</foreign>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>power</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in bondage</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 8</orig></choice> Eph. iii, 8-10 (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 9</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>recognised</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n11" target="#a11" n="11"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 10</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>gifts</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n12" target="#a12" n="12"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 113, n. 11</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>toward us</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
